Subject: [experimental] Stay-warped passes on two-layer eye targets

Unity's OpenXR plugin renders both eyes as the two layers of one multisampled
texture (single-pass instanced) and draws the resolved layers into a two-layer
swapchain. Under DXMT_STAY_WARPED a pass with up to two render-target layers
is now mapped (Metal applies the one-layer map to each layer), 8x MSAA is
accepted alongside 1x, 2x and 4x, and Sample, SampleLevel and Load on 2D array
textures (multisampled too: Unity resolves 8x MSAA with Load) are translated
like those on 2D textures, so the draw into the swapchain un-warps.
DXMT_STAY_WARPED_LAYERS=1 restores the one-layer rule.

The read flag moves to bit 9 so cached variants from earlier translations are
not reused. DXMT_DEBUG_DUMP_SLICE picks the layer the diagnostic frame dump
writes.

